The error reveals a logical inconsistency: `post-cycle-spin` is triggered by `pcr-cycle` ending, but `record-results` is a much later step in the same track. The validator is catching that the steps overlap in time because `record-results` starts before `post-cycle-spin` finishes.

The issue is that `post-cycle-spin` and `add-loading-dye` are both triggered relative to the PCR cycle, which ends at t=8580s, but `record-results` is at the very end of the protocol (after gel imaging). The track ordering in my JSON was misleading; I need to ensure strict sequential ordering within each track.

Looking at the timeline:
- PCR cycle ends at 8580s
- `post-cycle-spin` starts at 8580s, ends at 8610s
- `add-loading-dye` starts at 8610s, ends at 8880s
- `load-wells` waits for both `remove-comb` (which happens much earlier in gel-prep) and `thaw-ladder` (which is ready by 2400s), so it starts when `add-loading-dye` ends at 8880s
- `run-gel` starts at 9360s (8880 + 480), ends at 11760s
- `image-gel` starts at 11760s, ends at 12060s
- `record-results` starts at 12060s, ends at 12660s

The validator is correct: there is no overlap if I trace through properly. Let me re-examine the error message. It says `record-results` ends at 8640s but `post-cycle-spin` starts at 8580s — that means the steps are out of order in the track definition, creating a logical conflict.

